course: dictionary
lesson: 4815
title: The hundredth: position and part
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Hundredth has two meanings. First, it is a position in order: the hundredth is the number 100, coming straight after the ninety-ninth.
explain: Second, it is a part. A hundredth is one of a hundred equal parts of something, written 1/100 or 0.01. «Owning 1 share out of 100 means owning 1 hundredth of it.»
explain: Use the words around it to tell which meaning you need. «The hundredth day of school» is a place in a count, so it means 100th. «One hundredth of a pound» is a piece, so it means 1/100.
fact: Hundredth means 100th in order, as in the hundredth day of school.
fact: A hundredth is one of 100 equal parts, written 1/100 or 0.01.
fact: In 3.45, the 5 is in the hundredths place.
fact: A penny is one hundredth of a pound.
fact: One centimetre is one hundredth of a metre, so there are 100 centimetres in a metre.
exercise: In 3.45, which digit is in the hundredths place? | 4 | 3 | There is no digit in the hundredths place | *5
exercise: One penny is what fraction of a pound? | 1/1000 | *1/100 | 1/2 | 1/10
exercise: Which number comes straight before the hundredth? | Hundred and first | Ninetieth | *Ninety-ninth | Tenth
test: «One centimetre is one hundredth of a metre.» How many centimetres are in one metre? | 50 | *100 | 10 | 1000
test: «Owning 1 share out of 100 means owning 1 hundredth of it.» What part of the company do you own with 1 share? | 1 half | 10 hundredths | 1 tenth | *1 hundredth
exam: A stopwatch shows 0.01 seconds. What fraction of a second is that? | 10/10 | *1/100 | 1/10 | 1/1000
